PIN (unenforced invariant): a `!` branch must NOT discharge an OUTER obligation.
an outer obligation.

`! each *T<!state>` promises "discharge exactly once" via a branch that fires
0-to-N times — incoherent. Must be rejected at the SIGNATURE level (parser or
shape-checker), NOT by inspecting any body. Currently SILENTLY ACCEPTED (this
test expects FRONTEND_COMPILE_ERROR and gets clean compilation instead).

Symmetric note: resume-CREATE (`! make x -> *R<state!>`) IS coherent (one
create per firing, handed to the proc) — only payload-DISCHARGE of an outer
obligation is forbidden. The rejection must distinguish the two.

Build target: reject `<!state>` discharge-marker on a `kind == .effect` branch
payload. Companion to the obligation-tracking that already works for the
balanced case (see 400_100 PASS / 400_103 correct-reject).
